  message: "DONE in PR #2043 (dev 94b03ded17; lab /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/self_audit_11032026/jizam_*). CAUSE: the guard adjudicated the Python analyzer's RAW edges while the cron adjudicates them after three pipeline stages: (1) the tier filter, which drops the DERIVED scip/_generated/scip_pb2.py (tier 4 by the _pb2.py rule) with every edge touching it, leaving the rust-analyzer package's cross-package call as the unresolved module slot the cron names, where over raw edges the file counted as analysed and _is_analyzed_module suppressed the call as first-party; (2) boundary synthesis's id remap (ADR-0036 ruling 2), which normalises a dangling id's kind slot to external_symbol, the only terminal besides unresolved that _external_call_sites admits, so the analyzer's :attribute module_attr_ref dsts for timezone.utc / Select.BLANK (the #2036 from-imported chains) were invisible to the guard and counted by the cron; (3) the orchestrator's file-symbol synthesis (WI-ramuv/WI-dagif), without which a dropped file's import edge has no node to be dropped with. FIX: analyzer_edges runs the three through the pipeline's own functions; the tier filter is lifted from run_survey into hypergumbo_core/tier_filter.py (apply_tier_filter) so both callers share one copy. BEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE: the fixed guard on a worktree at acf67df4cb (the tree the cron withheld on) exits 1 naming hypergumbo_core.scip._generated.scip_pb2 and textual.widgets.Select (datetime.timezone granted since #2042), 46,029 edges from 71,539 raw, 31 s; on dev after #2042 exits 0. Lift parity: the refactored code surveying the same worktree reproduces the old map exactly (63,894 nodes same ids, 255,685 edges, per-type counts, tiers, tier_filtered_files); verify-claims drift OK, 18 unchanged. Tests: TestThePipelinesOwnPopulation (attribute read withholds; external_symbol terminal; a protoc-shaped import-time-defined _pb2 module is dropped with its edges, withholds naming p._generated.gen_pb2, a grant turns it green) and test_tier_filter.py; four of five new guard tests were red on the old guard. Bisect note: the scip_pb2 half predates #2036 (red at its parent), the two attribute slots arrived with #2036."  # 7064
